{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789646970,"nonce":"BDlEVkwjI4szb1ZeUpUwOOazvyg=","title":"Unreachable HIR blocks retain phi edges and block OSR","message":"The function-level reachability DCE skips unused functions, but the optimized HIR pipeline does not remove basic blocks disconnected from a function entry. In nbody_modified advance, the pre-opt HIR has 169 blocks and no dead orphans; the post-opt HIR has 313 blocks, including 17 non-entry blocks with no incoming path. Their stale phi incoming edges make OSR layout reject the outer loop as RegionHasExternalEntry. Prune unreachable blocks using terminator edges after optimization and remove their predecessor and phi entries. Keep real external paths into inner loops rejected.","files":null}]}